++Heap texture copies back to tiled bytes use a tile-coordinate dispatch for each
++level when every single-sample level has 4-, 8- or 16-byte elements and fits the
++device's dispatch limits. Each level retains its own shape and descriptor set.
++The original image transfer, staging padding, copy-back ranges and independent
++writer merges remain in place. Multi-level input, smaller elements and unsupported
++grids retain the generic conversion.
